{
  "_notes": [
    "Checkpoint [Data East, 1991]",
    "2026-02-14 added by Tom Collins <tom@scorbit.io>",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E46 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum stored at 0x1EFE (checksum8_sum, not",
    "complemented), the scheme measured live on tmnt_200 (see that map): the block runs from 0x1E00 to",
    "the byte before the 0xFF fill, which on this game is 0x1E46. Verified against saved ckpt_a17 images from both cabinets.",
    "A write that changes an adjustment without updating 0x1EFE is reset to factory at the next boot;",
    "0x1DDF is the ROM's derived free-play-in-effect flag, re-derived from 0x1E04 at boot.",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E46 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum (complement false) at 0x1EFE; see README.md in maps/dataeast."
  ],
